Z||000009||RDosdorian||08-14-2001||12:30 PM||||NOS3800....It's an 88GT 5-Speed with a 95 LT1 in it.  On the 1/4 mile it pulls hard through 3rd.  I hit 4th and it just slips.  I am told it is because of the horsepower the motor is producing at that point.  The clutch is Archies Centerforce.  I have been in contact with Archie and we are working on a solution.  I just have to have the time to pull the clutch and see whats going on.  As for my actual time (with no power in 4th.)  I mean I actually hit 4th.  I had NO power, so I coasted from the time I hit 4th through the timing lights.  I ran 13.9 at 80mph.  So again, with those numbers, I think a low 12 is in my future.  At that point, I will get kicked off the track due to specific safety requirements necessary when going that speed. (rollbar, 5 point harnesses, etc.)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.goldengatefieros.org/RDosdorian_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
